.TH FCNTL 2
.SH NAME
fcntl \- manipulate an open descriptor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <fcntl.h>
.sp
.BI "int fcntl(int fd, int command, ...);"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Astia supports
.BR F_DUPFD,
.BR F_DUPFD_CLOEXEC,
.BR F_GETFD,
.BR F_SETFD,
.BR F_GETFL
and
.BR F_SETFL .
Descriptor flags are per descriptor: setting
.B FD_CLOEXEC
does not change aliases made by
.BR dup (2).
Status flags are per open file description and therefore are shared by
duplicates.  The supported status flags are
.B O_APPEND
and
.BR O_NONBLOCK .
.SH RETURN VALUE
The result is the new descriptor, a flag word, or zero on success; on error
.B -1
is returned and
.B errno
is set.
